# {{ project_name }}

PySpark job deployed on Databricks (DBR {{ databricks_runtime }} LTS, Python {{ python_version }}) with Databricks Asset Bundles.

## Prerequisites

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- Java {{ java_version }} (for local Spark)
- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/) ≥ 0.218, authenticated against `{{ databricks_host }}`

## Getting started

```bash
make install                # uv sync --extra dev
uv run pre-commit install
make test                   # unit tests on a local Spark + Delta session
```

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/transformations/` | Pure DataFrame → DataFrame functions, unit-tested |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/io/` | Unity Catalog / Delta readers and writers |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/jobs/` | Jobs wiring I/O and transformations |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/conf/` | `base.yaml` + per-env overlays (`dev`, `staging`, `prod`) |
| `resources/` | Databricks job definitions |

Add a job by creating a module in `jobs/` exposing `run(spark, cfg)` and registering it in `_JOBS` in `main.py`.

## Configuration

`load_config(env)` deep-merges `conf/base.yaml` with `conf/<env>.yaml`. The `spark` section is applied
as runtime Spark confs at startup (keys without the `spark.` prefix).

## Deployment

| Target | How |
| --- | --- |
| dev | `make deploy-dev` then `make run-dev` (resources prefixed with your username) |
| staging | automatic on push to `main` |
| prod | automatic on `v*` tag, gated by the `production` GitHub environment |

CI authenticates with a service principal (OAuth M2M): set `DATABRICKS_HOST`, `DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID`
and `DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET` in the `staging` and `production` GitHub environments.

## Updating from the template

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```
